# Custom response headers for Workers static assets.
#
# This file is copied from public/ into dist-site/ by `npm run build:site` and
# is consumed by Cloudflare Workers static assets (not served as a file). The
# rules apply to asset responses, including responses returned by
# `env.ASSETS.fetch()` from worker/staging.ts and worker/index.ts.
#
# HTML is deliberately absent: it keeps the Workers default
# `Cache-Control: public, max-age=0, must-revalidate` so a new deploy is picked
# up on the next navigation. Never add a long-lived rule for `/` or `/*.html`.
#
# Vite fingerprints every file in /assets (name-<hash>.js|css), so a one-year
# immutable cache is safe: a new build produces a new filename. Font filenames
# are stable (not hashed), so replacing a face must also rename the file (or
# add a version query) or clients will keep the old bytes for a year.

/assets/*
  Cache-Control: public, max-age=31536000, immutable

/fonts/*
  Cache-Control: public, max-age=31536000, immutable
